  "method": "FP32 and official MLX BF16 (0.32.4) rows were produced once for the 144-token sequence with --rows 31..127; native used tokens[:N] with prompt:N for N in 32..128 step 4 (25 prompt lengths) for baseline and --tiled-attention. tools/lfm3/prompt_row_sweep.py.",
  "finding": "Across 25 boundary rows baseline, tiled attention and official BF16 have indistinguishable mean distance to FP32 (mean RMS 0.0390 / 0.0389 / 0.0402; mean max 0.185 / 0.186 / 0.196; mean top-20 probability max 3.9e-4 / 4.1e-4 / 4.7e-4). Tiled attention RMS exceeded official BF16 in 11/25 rows; baseline in 9/25. No top-1 miss in any route. The N=128 single-row failure is within the per-row spread (official BF16 per-row RMS ranges 0.0296-0.0757). Rows come from one sequence and are correlated, so this is not independent-prompt evidence."
